---
/**
 * Sharply seasonal: the November–December spike is most of this page's year, and
 * the buyer is frequently NOT a golfer — which is the segment's core insight
 * (playbook-sim-venue.md §1). So the copy is written for someone buying for a
 * golfer, not for a golfer.
 *
 * Two things this page must do that the current site does not: put "check a
 * balance" on the same page as "buy", and say whether one card works at both
 * venues. The second is unknown, so it is marked.
 *
 * ⚠️ Two gift-card vendors are in circulation on the current site — Square on the
 * live pages, Toast on an orphaned old homepage. Square is the one wired up in
 * globalData.external and the one used here. Confirm Toast is dead before launch.
 *
 * ── "THE DETAILS" IS A GAP TABLE NOW, NOT A STUB (FW-4013) ─────────────────
 *
 * This section used to open "STUB — what a buyer needs before they will click,
 * and none of it is published today", followed by a bulleted brief addressed to
 * us. It rendered in production, under the heading "The details", to the exact
 * person it was describing.
 *
 * Every bullet in it was a QUESTION THE BUYER IS ASKING — what amounts, does it
 * cover food, how fast does it arrive, does it work at the other venue. Those
 * are the gap system's first mark, not a stub: they are customer-facing on
 * purpose, they are typeset like a published answer would be, and they say
 * plainly that we do not have the answer rather than pretending the question was
 * never asked. Somebody about to spend money in December is better served by
 * four marked absences and a phone number than by a confident silence.
 *
 * What is genuinely OURS — expiry, whether a card pays for a membership or a
 * LinksFlex block, physical cards, killing the Toast vendor — went to a
 * `StubNote` and shows on staging only.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookButton from '../components/venue/BookButton.astro';
import GapCell from '../components/venue/GapCell.astro';
import StubNote from '../components/venue/StubNote.astro';
import { globalData } from '../data/global';

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'Golf Gift Cards — The Links, Lakeville & Stillwater',
  metaDescription:
    'Buy a The Links gift card online for indoor golf in Lakeville or Stillwater, MN — or check a balance in a couple of clicks.',
};

/** Why this is a good present, written for the non-golfer buying it. */
const whyItWorks = [
  [
    'They do not have to be good',
    'A bay is booked by the hour and the difficulty is a setting. Someone who has never held a club has a decent night; so does a single-figure handicap.',
  ],
  [
    'They pick the night',
    'A bay is booked by the hour, so it fits a Tuesday evening as easily as a Saturday afternoon. Nothing has to be scheduled at the point you buy it.',
  ],
  [
    'It works in February',
    'Which is the point. An outdoor golf gift bought in December is a gift they cannot open for four months.',
  ],
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold lg:text-5xl">Gift cards</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-inkMuted">
      An hour in a bay, bought online in a couple of clicks. They pick the night.
    </p>

    {/* 1. Buy and check balance, together, at the top. */}
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded border-2 border-primary p-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Buy a gift card</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          Gift cards are sold through Square. Choose an amount and pay; Square handles the rest.
        </p>
        <a
          href={globalData.external.giftCardBuy}
          class="mt-6 inline-block rounded bg-primary px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-surface transition hover:opacity-90"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          data-analytics="giftcard:buy"
        >
          Buy a gift card <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span class="sr-only">(opens our gift card page in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded border-2 border-ink/15 p-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Check a balance</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          Been sitting in a wallet since last Christmas? Enter the number and it will tell you what is left on it.
        </p>
        <a
          href={globalData.external.giftCardBalance}
          class="mt-6 inline-block rounded border-2 border-current px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-ink transition hover:bg-ink hover:text-surface"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          data-analytics="giftcard:balance"
        >
          Check my balance <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span class="sr-only">(opens our gift card balance page in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* 2. Written for the buyer, who often does not play golf. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Buying for a golfer, and you are not one</h2>
      <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          whyItWorks.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="text-lg font-semibold">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-inkMuted">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    {/* 3. The questions a gift-card buyer asks that nobody answers. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">The details</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose-page text-inkMuted">
        Four questions a buyer reasonably asks that the venue does not publish answers to. We are not going to guess at
        any of them with your money on the line, so here they are, marked. Either venue will answer them on the phone —
        the numbers are on the <a href="/contact/" class="font-semibold underline">contact page</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <GapCell
          label="Denominations"
          state="notSet"
          size="name"
          reason="Whether you choose the amount or pick from a fixed set, and whether there is a minimum, is not published anywhere the venue controls."
        />
        <GapCell
          label="Food and drink, or bay time only"
          state="notSet"
          size="name"
          reason="Nothing the venue publishes says either way, and it is the first thing the person opening it will try to do with it. Worth a phone call before you buy if a meal is part of the present."
        />
        <GapCell
          label="How it arrives"
          state="notSet"
          size="name"
          reason="Whether the card comes by email, how quickly, and whether it can be used the same day is not published — which is the whole question if you are buying on 23 December."
        />
        <GapCell
          label="Works at both venues"
          state="notSet"
          size="name"
          reason="Lakeville and Stillwater run separate booking accounts, and whether one card is good at both has never been stated. If the golfer is a Stillwater one, ask us first."
        />
      </div>
      <StubNote
        class="mt-6"
        needs="Also to confirm, and none of it is a buyer's question: expiry (if any), whether a card can be used against a membership or a LinksFlex block, whether physical cards exist for someone who wants something to hand over, and confirmation that the Toast vendor on the orphaned old homepage is dead. Note that this page used to claim a card covered food and drink as well as bay time; nothing the venue publishes supports that, so it is now marked as a gap. Do not put the claim back without a source."
      />
    </section>

    {
      /* 4. Seasonality. The featured-offer slot leans on this in Nov–Dec
       (strategy.md §5) — this section is the landing point for it. */
    }
    <section class="mt-section rounded bg-surface p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">If it is November or December</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Winter is the season this whole business exists for — league nights, work parties, and no golf outdoors. If you
        are giving one as a Christmas present, suggest they put the date in as soon as they have one, rather than
        leaving it until a Saturday in February happens to be free.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Planning a work party rather than a present? <a href="/events/" class="font-semibold underline"
          >Events and parties</a
        > is the page you want.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* Every page ends in a transactional CTA (playbook-core.md §6). */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Or just bring them</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        A bay is priced by the hour, not the head. Book one and take them with you — cheaper than most presents and you
        get to come too.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a
          href={globalData.external.giftCardBuy}
          class="inline-block rounded bg-primary px-8 py-4 text-lg font-semibold text-surface transition hover:opacity-90"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          data-analytics="giftcard:buy-footer"
        >
          Buy a gift card <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span class="sr-only">(opens our gift card page in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
        <BookButton size="lg" variant="outline" />
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
